WEBVTT

00:19:58.255 --> 00:20:00.640
because I really love to be able
to talk to people

00:20:00.664 --> 00:20:03.245
about what they actually think and feel.

00:20:03.269 --> 00:20:05.208
For me, small talk is the kryptonite.

00:20:05.232 --> 00:20:07.943
So, the amazing thing
since I've written this book is,

00:20:07.967 --> 00:20:09.787
I almost never have to do small talk,

00:20:09.811 --> 00:20:14.585
because people will now talk to me
about whatever it is

00:20:14.609 --> 00:20:16.712
that is making them feel vulnerable.

00:20:16.736 --> 00:20:18.787
And so, we kind of get to the heart of it.

00:20:18.811 --> 00:20:21.860
CA: But based on that,
isn't it possible that,

00:20:21.884 --> 00:20:25.046
rather than saying a third to a half
of people are introverts,

00:20:25.070 --> 00:20:29.341
you might almost say that
the majority of people, at times,

00:20:29.365 --> 00:20:32.991
feel intensely the kinds
of feelings that introverts feel?